{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>A yovel it is.</b> This year is distinguished from all other years by being designated with a name of its own. And what is its name? Its name is yovel, on account of the sounding of the shofar — this is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Leviticus 25:10). And so is the opinion of the commentators, from the language of \"when the yovel sounds a long blast\" (Exodus 19:13), \"the yovelim horns\" (Joshua 6:4). But it is not clear to me, because of \"it shall be for you\" — for what reason should the verse say about the year, \"it is a sounding, it shall be for you, and you shall return\"? Perhaps the verse says \"a yovel it is\" — designated with this name that I have called it, and \"it shall be for you\" means for all of you: made known by the sounding that you sound in it, to proclaim its significance, that you shall return in it, each man to his possession and each man to his family. And similarly, \"a yovel it is, the fiftieth year it shall be for you\" (Leviticus 25:11) — that it shall be for you a yovel in which you shall neither sow nor reap; that is, known by name for being thus. And all of this is not correct in my eyes, for the meaning of \"the yovelim horns\" is the horns of rams, and likewise the Targum of Yonatan renders \"a shofar of ram's horn,\" and so in the Gemara (Rosh HaShanah 26a): what does this word yovela mean? It is a word for ram, for in Arabic they call a ram yovela. And the shofar on Yom HaKippurim is not specifically required to be from a ram, but all shofars are valid for it. And according to the opinion of our Mishnah (ibid.) and all the Tanna'im, its commandment is with one of rams — if so, why is the year called the year of the ram? And Rabbi Abraham ibn Ezra said that yovel has the sense of sending away. In my opinion, Scripture did not call it yovel on account of the sounding, but on account of the freedom (deror), for it did not mention this name in the first verse it stated: \"and you shall sound the shofar, a teru'ah\" — but rather it said, \"and you shall proclaim deror in the land to all its inhabitants,\" that they shall all be free men to dwell wherever they wish. And it said, \"a yovel it is,\" for in it every man is brought (yuvall) to his possession and to his family — \"his feet will carry him from afar to sojourn\" (Isaiah 23:7). And this language was used in many contexts: \"a gift brought (yuvall) to YHWH of Hosts\" (Isaiah 18:7), and it says, \"and it sends out its roots by a channel (yval)\" (Jeremiah 17:8), \"streams of flowing (yivlei) waters\" (Isaiah 30:25) — these are the deep channels where the waters are brought (yuvallu). \"And the land shall give its yield (yevulah)\" (Leviticus 26:4), \"and there is no yield (yevul) in the vines\" (Habakkuk 3:17) — the concept of bringing forth as well, just as produce (tevu'ah) is called. And so in Aramaic, \"and he walked quickly\" (Numbers 17:11) is translated \"ve'ovel bifreia.\" And the meaning of \"a yovel it is, it shall be for you\" will be: it is a bringing (hava'ah), and so it shall be for all of you, for you shall come and return, each man to his possession and each man to his family. And it returned and said, \"a yovel it is, the fiftieth year it shall be for you\" (Leviticus 25:11) — that the fiftieth year shall be for you for a yovel, not for anything else, and you shall not sow and you shall not reap, but it shall be holy, and you shall return each man to his possession, for it to be for all of you a yovel as its name. And by way of truth, \"deror\" is from the language of \"a generation goes and a generation comes (dor holekh v'dor ba)\" (Ecclesiastes 1:4), and likewise \"yovel\" — that it returns to the yovel where its root is, and it shall be for you:"], :book :leviticus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "Where Ramban quotes Targum Yonatan and the Talmud, the Aramaic/Aramaic-transliterated phrases are preserved as they appear in his Hebrew text with minimal glossing, since the argument turns on the linguistic forms themselves."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:59:55.168441106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}